WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:06.539
Riley downshifted and pedaled hard along the straightaway.

2
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:15.533
Dirt and mud spattered her in the face, stinging her skin, but all she could see was the trail.

3
00:00:15.534 --> 00:00:19.159
At the end of the straightaway, the track made a hard turn.

4
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:26.180
Riley hit the turn, her back tire sliding in the dirt and throwing her off balance.

5
00:00:26.181 --> 00:00:32.941
She stood up on the pedals and pulled back with her body, steadying the bike around the curve.

6
00:00:32.942 --> 00:00:38.606
In front of her, the trail took a fast dip down a hill and then traveled upward again.

7
00:00:38.607 --> 00:00:42.020
Riley thought she caught a glimpse of Quinn up ahead.

8
00:00:42.021 --> 00:00:49.585
Quinn had started thirty seconds before Riley, and she'd lost some time, but Riley had lost time too.

9
00:00:49.586 --> 00:00:57.752
"I just have to beat Quinn's overall time," Riley reminded herself. "I don't have to beat her across the finish line."

10
00:00:57.753 --> 00:01:03.426
Still, it would feel wonderful to cross the finish line ahead of Quinn!

11
00:01:03.427 --> 00:01:08.388
There was another straightaway after the hill—it was perfect for a fast sprint.

12
00:01:08.389 --> 00:01:13.976
Riley barreled down the track, her leg muscles burning.

13
00:01:13.977 --> 00:01:19.721
When she got over the hill, Quinn was ahead of her in the distance, but closer now. "Woo-hoo!"

14
00:01:19.722 --> 00:01:25.401
Riley thought. "Watch out, Quinn—here I come!" Quinn

15
00:01:25.402 --> 00:01:29.644
glanced over her shoulder and spotted Riley. She

16
00:01:29.645 --> 00:01:36.318
pedaled furiously and disappeared so fast, Riley was stunned. She

17
00:01:36.319 --> 00:01:41.959
couldn't help being impressed—Quinn sure knew what she was doing on her bike. "I

18
00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:51.374
do too," Riley told herself. She crouched low over the handlebars, pushing herself harder. Riley

19
00:01:51.375 --> 00:02:00.868
took several more curves easily, leaning into them confidently and holding her balance. A

20
00:02:00.869 --> 00:02:10.282
jump was coming up—the final one. She shifted gears, throwing a burst of speed into her bike. As

21
00:02:10.283 --> 00:02:18.442
she approached the jump, she gripped the handlebars and pedaled hard, rising in her seat to balance the bike. She

22
00:02:18.443 --> 00:02:24.224
sailed over the jump in a perfect arc. "Yes!"

23
00:02:24.225 --> 00:02:28.595
she hollered with delight. Her

24
00:02:28.596 --> 00:02:36.167
wheels landed together with a satisfying thump, and then Riley was pedaling furiously again. Soon

25
00:02:36.168 --> 00:02:42.496
she was closing the gap again, drawing closer to Quinn. As

26
00:02:42.497 --> 00:02:49.412
Riley pulled closer, she thought she saw Quinn's back wheel was wobbling. "Yikes,"

27
00:02:49.413 --> 00:02:53.568
Riley thought. "That could be dangerous." "Go!"

28
00:02:53.569 --> 00:02:58.497
People standing on the sidelines roared at the girls. "Keep

29
00:02:58.498 --> 00:03:03.894
up your speed, Riley!" somebody yelled. "Focus!" Quinn

30
00:03:03.895 --> 00:03:17.145
stood up on her bike, and with a last burst of speed, pulled way ahead of Riley. Riley stood up too, pumping hard. Minutes

31
00:03:17.146 --> 00:03:28.304
later the two riders zipped toward the finish line. Quinn crossed first, with Riley following seconds later. Riley

32
00:03:28.305 --> 00:03:37.193
hadn't beaten Quinn over the finish line, but she'd scored one important victory—a better time than Quinn's! "I

33
00:03:37.194 --> 00:03:39.991
did it!" she thought. Riley

34
00:03:39.992 --> 00:03:47.020
crossed her fingers, hoping that her ride had also been good enough to beat all the other girls in the junior division. Quinn

35
00:03:47.021 --> 00:03:56.259
had turned off the track and thrown her bike down. Now she was collapsed on the grass. Riley

36
00:03:56.260 --> 00:04:04.426
rode straight to her parents and Jordan, who was doing her best to jump and clap while on crutches. Riley

37
00:04:04.427 --> 00:04:10.846
dropped her bike, and Jordan grabbed her in a crushing hug. "I

38
00:04:10.847 --> 00:04:17.259
knew you could nail those jumps!" Jordan kept yelling. "What a great ride!" "I

39
00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:24.242
should have made that one jump," Riley said after her sister and parents had stopped congratulating her. "But I

40
00:04:24.243 --> 00:04:31.821
had a really good fall—just like you taught me, Jordan—and that helped me stay in the race." Delaney came

41
00:04:31.822 --> 00:04:41.323
over to high-five Riley. "Way to go," he said. "You were awesome." Coach Adams

42
00:04:41.324 --> 00:04:50.975
joined them. "Nice run, Riley!" he said. "I'm especially impressed at your recovery from that fall." "Thanks," Riley

43
00:04:50.976 --> 00:04:56.308
replied. "I was pretty worried there for a second." "Well, you

44
00:04:56.309 --> 00:05:03.641
should be proud of your ride," Coach Adams said. "You showed a lot of guts and determination on the track." "I'll be

45
00:05:03.642 --> 00:05:08.806
prouder of my ride if I make the team," Riley said, grinning. "We'll see,"

46
00:05:08.807 --> 00:05:17.551
Coach replied. "We'll announce the new team members after all the riders have finished their tryouts." * *

47
00:05:17.552 --> 00:05:26.433
* While everyone waited for the last riders to finish, Riley went over to the grassy spot and dropped down beside

48
00:05:26.434 --> 00:05:30.199
Quinn. The other girl hadn't moved since she finished her

49
00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:36.031
ride. Quinn looked at her. "What do you want?" she asked in a tired

50
00:05:36.032 --> 00:05:45.431
voice. "To congratulate you," Riley said. "That was a fantastic ride. And you made a really nice recovery from that

51
00:05:45.432 --> 00:05:50.684
fall." Quinn narrowed her eyes suspiciously. "I doubt I made the

52
00:05:50.685 --> 00:05:58.604
team." Riley shrugged. "We'll see, but I think you and I are going to be junior Blue

53
00:05:58.605 --> 00:06:05.919
Demons." "I'm not so sure about me," Quinn mumbled. "But you had a really strong

54
00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:13.841
ride." "Thanks," Riley said. "How did you fall behind before that big jump? Did something happen on the

55
00:06:13.842 --> 00:06:21.316
track?" Quinn closed her eyes, sighing. "If I tell you, you'll just mock me for being a stupid

56
00:06:21.317 --> 00:06:25.418
snob." "No, I won't," Riley said. "Why would I do

57
00:06:25.419 --> 00:06:33.417
that?" "Because my fabulous, custom-designed bike has a fatal flaw," Quinn went on. "Its dumb

58
00:06:33.418 --> 00:06:35.934
rider." Riley was confused.

59
00:06:35.935 --> 00:06:37.820
"Huh?" Quinn looked

60
00:06:37.821 --> 00:06:45.048
away. "I was so sure my bike was perfect that I didn't bother doing a pre-race check. Some of the bolts were

61
00:06:45.049 --> 00:06:50.038
loose." "Oh . . ." Riley murmured. "That was pretty dumb,

62
00:06:50.039 --> 00:06:56.220
Quinn." "My bike felt strange when I started," Quinn went on, "but I thought it was the soft track.

63
